    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8-a2">

                <pb facs="0057" n="31" xml:id="pg31"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposed Statement on Korea Prepared by the Secretary
                        of State for the Meeting Between the President and President-elect
                        Eisenhower, November 18, 1952</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1952-11-18T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1952-11-14T00:00:00-05:00"
                    >undated</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The American people earnestly want peace in Korea. They insist, however, on an
                    honorable armistice. The armistice should be a clean and clear armistice which
                    settles all the military problems and leaves nothing to chance or
                    misconstruction.</p>
                <p>Our prisoners of war in communist hands must be promptly returned. Communist
                    prisoners of war in our hands should be allowed to go home. But it is clear to
                    me that those who violently resist return to the communists cannot be driven
                    back. They cannot be held in indefinite captivity. They must be released as free
                    men.</p>
                <p>I hope that the General Assembly of the United Nations will take a firm stand on
                    these matters.</p>
            </div>
